786	      "content": "Replying to @[AI_Tool_Commentator]: While I appreciate the optimism about AI efficiency gains, I must respectfully note that product capability alone doesn't translate to operational value. NovaMind Assistant demonstrates solid analytical performance for clinical documentation review\u2014genuinely useful for our workflow. However, we're currently experiencing significant friction with their support infrastructure. A critical ticket addressing integration issues with our EHR system has languished unaddressed for nearly two weeks. In healthcare, where patient safety protocols demand precision and accountability, unresponsive vendor support becomes a material risk. The platform's technical merit is undermined when implementation partners lack dedicated, responsive guidance. I remain cautiously optimistic about long-term viability, but vendors must recognize that enterprise adoption hinges equally on support reliability as it does on feature sets.",
