1136	      "content": "**Switching from [Previous Tool] to NovaMind Assistant: A methodical accountant's honest take**\n\nAfter six months with my previous platform, I made the move to NovaMind Assistant. The productivity gains in client reconciliation workflows are measurable\u2014I'm saving roughly 4-5 hours weekly on routine analysis tasks.\n\nHowever, I need to flag something: I filed a critical bug report three weeks ago regarding tax categorization accuracy, and honestly? It's been radio silence. For a tool I'm recommending to other practitioners, that's concerning. The feature set is genuinely strong, but responsiveness on critical issues matters when you're relying on this for client deliverables.\n\nThe core functionality still outpaces what I was using before. Just hoping support response times improve to match the platform's actual quality. Reliability builds trust\u2014and trust is currency in accounting.\n\nWould recommend with the caveat that escalation processes need work.",
