1462	{'post_id': 281, 'day': 126, 'content': "Has anyone else noticed a tangible shift in their billable hours since integrating NovaMind Assistant into their practice management workflow?\n\nI've been methodical about tracking this—six weeks in, and I'm reclaiming roughly 4-5 hours weekly on document analysis and precedent research. For a solo practice, that translates directly to either expanded capacity or improved margins. The assistant's context retention across complex case files has eliminated the usual back-and-forth clarifications I'd normally need.\n\nNot without friction points (the export formatting could be tighter), but the ROI calculation here is straightforward. Curious if other legal professionals are seeing similar patterns, or if your experience has differed.", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None}
1463	{'post_id': 282, 'day': 126, 'content': "**Reconsidering NovaMind Assistant After Recent Support Gaps**\n\nI've relied on NovaMind for clinical documentation workflows over the past year, and the core functionality remains solid. However, my experience has noticeably deteriorated lately. Response times from their support team have stretched from hours to days—problematic when patient workflows are affected. A critical issue I escalated three weeks ago remains unresolved despite multiple follow-ups.\n\nThe product itself handles our documentation needs capably, but enterprise-level support seems to have fallen away. For healthcare practitioners where reliability is non-negotiable, this inconsistency is concerning. I'm evaluating alternatives that match NovaMind's capabilities with more responsive support infrastructure.\n\nWorth trying if you have modest support needs. Less so if you require the responsiveness this industry demands.", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None}
1464	{'post_id': 283, 'day': 126, 'content': "**Paying premium rates for NovaMind Assistant, but apparently getting budget-tier support.** Three department handoffs on a single ticket and counting—at this price point, I'd expect support that knows which team actually owns what. The AI does solid work, but when something breaks, you're funding a support shuffle, not solutions. Disappointing ROI on the service tier, frankly.", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None}
