284	{'post_id': 497, 'day': 196, 'content': "Been relying on NovaMind Assistant for about three months now in my solo practice, and what's impressed me most isn't just the output quality—it's the consistency. In legal work, you can't afford flaky tools. I need something that's going to be there when I'm prepping briefs at 11 PM or drafting client memos on tight deadlines.\n\nNovaMind hasn't let me down once. Zero downtime issues, no random hiccups mid-session. For someone like me who bills by the hour, that reliability translates directly to efficiency. The research summaries it generates are thorough enough that I'm catching nuances I might've missed doing it manually, but it knows when to flag ambiguities that need my review.\n\nNot the cheapest option out there, but for early-career solo practitioners who can't risk losing billable hours to technical problems, it's worth every penny. Would definitely recommend if you're methodical about your work and actually care about uptime.", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None}
