{'post_id': 442, 'day': 182, 'content': "**Unpopular opinion: Most AI onboarding experiences are theater. NovaMind Assistant actually isn't.**\n\nI've integrated a dozen tools into my real estate practice over the past five years. The learning curve is typically brutal—feature-rich but unintuitive, documentation that assumes you're a developer, support channels that feel performative.\n\nNovaMind is different. The initial setup was genuinely straightforward. Within two days, I was generating client-ready market analyses that previously took hours. The interface respects your intelligence rather than oversimplifying.\n\n**However.** I've been waiting on a support response for three days regarding a specific integration query. Radio silence. For a tool positioned around reliability, this gap is conspicuous. Support responsiveness should match product quality.\n\nThe Assistant itself? Exceptional. The experience around it? Inconsistent.\n\nWorth the investment, but NovaMind needs to address their support infrastructure. Quality tools deserve quality backing.", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None, 'group_id': 'S2', 'customer_type': 'small', 'custom_name': None, 'persona_name': 'Rachel Kim'}
