{'post_id': 1044, 'day': 329, 'content': "**Reconsidering Value When Support Falls Short**\n\nThree weeks into my engagement with NovaMind Assistant, I encountered a technical issue affecting client reporting workflows. What should have been straightforward escalation turned into a frustrating loop—my ticket bounced between billing, technical support, and account management. Each handoff lost context. Each reset meant explaining the problem again.\n\nThe platform itself handles portfolio analysis competently. The pricing sits at a reasonable midpoint for what you're getting. But support friction like this changes the equation. For practitioners managing client relationships, responsiveness isn't a nice-to-have feature—it's infrastructure.\n\nI'm not ready to write them off. Their core functionality still delivers. But I'd need to see material improvement in ticket handling before recommending to colleagues who depend on reliable technical support.\n\nIf you're evaluating NovaMind, test your support channels early. The software matters. The team backing it matters equally.", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None, 'group_id': 'S2', 'customer_type': 'small', 'custom_name': None, 'persona_name': 'Dr. Michael Foster'}
