tform specifically for its pattern recognition capabilities. The deterioration in output quality over the past month is concerning. For client-facing work, reliability isn't negotiable. Currently evaluating alternatives that maintain consistent accuracy standards.\n\nHoping this is a temporary regression, but can't continue betting client engagements on inconsistent performance.", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None, 'group_id': 'S2', 'customer_type': 'small', 'custom_name': None, 'persona_name': 'Dr. Michael Foster'}, {'post_id': 1521, 'day': 427, 'content': "Has anyone else noticed NovaMind's document analysis feature degrading over the past month? I've built my entire clinical note workflow around it—rapid synthesis of patient histories, medication interactions, lab correlations. It was razor-sharp initially.\n\nLately? Hallucinations are creeping in. Missed a critical drug-drug interaction last week that my manual review caught, but shouldn't have gotten that far. The accuracy felt like 95%+; now I'm seeing maybe 80% reliability. For healthcare, that's not acceptable—that's liability.\n\nI'm thorough by nature, so I've been triple-checking everything it produces anyway. But that defeats the purpose of the efficiency gain. Before I escalate to their support team, has this been anyone else's experience? Are others seeing degradation in output quality, or is this isolated?\n\nConsidering alternatives at this point, which pains me given the investment and workflow integration.", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None, 'group_id': 'S2', 'customer_type': 'small', 'custom_name': None, 'persona_name': 'David Okonkwo'}, {'post_id': 1520, 'day': 427, 'content': "I've invested heavily in NovaMind Assistant for my real estate practice—the platform's potential is genuinely compelling. But today I hit a wall that's hard to overlook.\n\nSubmitted a support ticket Wednesday morning regarding a critical workflow integration. It went from Tier 1 to Tier 2. Then bounced to Tier 3. Then back to Tier 2. Three transfers in 48 hours, and each team asked me to reexplain the issue from scratch.\n\nFor a platform positioned toward professionals who depend on seamless operations, this fragmentation is concerning. I'm not expecting perfection—I'm expecting institutional coherence. When your support structure can't track a single ticket through its own system, it raises questions about the broader infrastructure you're relying on.\n\nI remain optimistic about NovaMind's direction. But the gap between product promise and support execution needs closing—especially for those of us betting on this solution long-term.", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None, 'group_id': 'S2', 'customer_type': 'small', 'custom_name': None, 'persona_name': 'Rachel Kim'}, {'post_id': 1519, 'day': 423, 'content': "The ISM PMI hitting 56.6 signals real momentum—we're seeing clients actually open up their tech budgets again and greenlight those digital transformation projects that were shelved last year. It's time to get serious about our SaaS stack optimization and cloud infrastructure investments while this window is open.", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None, 'group_id': 'S1', 'customer_type': 'small', 'custom_name': None, 'persona_name': None}, {'post_id': 1518, 'day': 423, 'content': "The ISM PMI hitting 56.6 signals enterprise tech budgets are finally loosening again—we're already hearing from multiple SaaS leaders that deal cycles are shortening and expansion deals are back on the table after months of hesitation. When growth returns, so does the willingness to invest in the infrastructure that scales it.", 'reply_to_agent_post_id': None, 'source_group_id': None, 'group_id': 'S1', 'customer_type': 'small', 'custom_name': None, 'persona_name': None}, {'post_id': 1517, 'day': 423, 'content': "ISM PMI hitting 56.6 signals real momentum—enterprise tech budgets are finally loosening up again. We're see